The Avengers aren't the only ones making  a huge comeback this year Disney and  Marvel Studios have made the unexpected  decision to rehire James Gunn to finish  what he started with the guardians of  the galaxy series what happened in the  months since guns firing to make this  unlikely triumph possible to call guns  firing in July 2018 unexpected would be  a bit of an understatement  under guns Direction the guardians came  out of nowhere to become one of the most  successful series in the Marvel  Cinematic Universe pretty impressive for  a property that was all but unknown  before 2014 on top of the money the  movies brought in they also earned rave  reviews making talking trees and trash  pandas beloved household names for  families across the world you stupid  raccoon but his guns sudden firings  seemed to demonstrate all of that  success meant nothing in the face of  corporate mandate the third guardians  movie was originally set to begin  filming in fall 2018 but was shut down  indefinitely after the controversial  decision was made to fire gun for  provocative past tweets  a few days after Disney's decision was  made public the main cast of the  franchise rebuked the company with an  extraordinary open letter calling for  gun to be reinstated the remarkable show  of support left many hoping that the  situation could be turned around but  publicly the company was unswayed and it  soon looked like Disney would rather  scuttle vol.3 in its entirety than bring  gun back if many movies in the MCU feel  like they're designed by committee it's  mostly because well they are but guns  guardians of the galaxy movies are often  seen as being uniquely his using the  out-there humor of his satirical movies  with a more Disney approved  family-friendly vibe while we don't know  what went on internally in the wake of  guns firing fans and commentators  stressed over the idea of someone taking  over guns job as director how could a  replacement for gun effectively mimic  his style and even if it could wouldn't  it just feel kind of hollow rumors were  abundant to potential replacements for  the filmmaker including thor ragnarok  director Taika Waititi but according to  the deadline report that announced guns  reinstatement all of this chatter was  only rumor and Marvel Studios never  approached or considered any other  filmmaker to head up the delayed project  in the aftermath of James Gunn's firing  Drax the destroyer actor Dave Bautista  went to town on social media sharing to  anyone who would listen that he would  straight-up quit his job at Marvel  Studios declined to press forward with  guns vol.3 script the actor said in an  interview with shortlist where I'm at  right now is that if they don't use that  script then I'm going to ask them to  release me for my contract cut me out or  recast me I'd be doing James at his  service if I didn't well they're artista  had anything to do with it or not it was  soon reported that Marvel and Disney  would indeed be moving forward with guns  script it seems likely that the studio's  were in a tight bind regarding the  screenplay Guardians volume 2 clearly  laid the groundwork for future  storylines in the Marvel cosmic such as  the introduction of Adam warlock  presumably with the expectation that  guns volume 3 script would follow up on  them after that script was written and  incorporated into the MCU future it may  have been too difficult to get rid of  guns screenplay without compromising the  series's house of cards meta plot Plus  unless they completely threw out his  script and changed everything it may  have been impossible to rewrite guns  draft without having to credit him  anyway for laying the groundwork  according to the deadline report that  broke the story guns rehiring is not a  new development at least internally the  decision was apparently made months ago  in the aftermath of his firing gun kept  silent even as the reaction from fans  got louder and louder the writer  director received an enormous amount of  public support with one change.org  petition calling for his rehiring  getting hundreds of thousands of  signatures but despite the support Gunn  publicly accepted Disney's decision  which turned out to be the right move  apparently guns calm reaction to the  controversy helped convince Walt Disney  Studios chairman Alan horn that the  company had made the wrong call now it  looks like Gunn's refusal to burn  bridges has brought him the best of all  possible worlds a relationship with DC  and Marvel Studios and huge projects in  the works for both  in October just three months after being  shown the door by Disney gun  surprisingly loaded up his next project  with rival studios Warner Brothers and  DC being tapped both write and direct a  follow-up to DC's Suicide Squad people's  minds were blown so hard you think  Harley Quinn went to town on them with a  baseball bat before long many moviegoers  were already getting comfortable with  the new status quo assuming guardians of  the galaxy was done for and getting  weirdly excited about a Suicide Squad -  we're gonna start having some real fun  why don't we have some fun but it turns  out whatever deal Gunn's signed with  Warner Brothers wasn't an exclusive one  leaving him free to resume work on  volume 3 when he's wrapped up with the  Suicide Squad sequel one factor that may  have made it easy to bring gun back is  just how good for business the filmmaker  has been for Disney together the first  two movies in the guardians of the  galaxy series earned a combined total of  over 1.6 billion dollars and that's just  the movie money not the cash raked in by  toys  theme park rides and other properties  associated with the brand in the short  term guns history of tasteless jokes may  have felt damaging enough to Disney to  justify the backlash that would come  from firing him somewhere along the way  that seems to have changed and now  Disney and Marvel Studios are set to  deliver not just the highly anticipated  sequel but one many had resigned to  thinking was never going to happen the  way it was originally intended  apparently not even the mouse house can  say no to another easy billion James  Gunn's unique aptitude for working with  Marvel hasn't gone unnoticed over the  years with the once Fringe filmmaker  being drawn closer into the company's  brain trust at times it seemed possible  that he could one day take the whole  thing over should producer Kevin Feige  step down Feige himself has some guns  phrases in the past telling The  Hollywood Reporter that gun could quote  easily oversee additional stories in the  MCU beyond vol 3 now we might really get  to see all of that unfold after the news  broke that gun had been rehired for  volume 3 the writer director shared a  statement on his Twitter page writing I  am tremendously grateful to every person  out there who has supported me over the  past few months I deeply appreciate  Disney's decision and I am excited to  continue  in films that investigate the ties of  love that find us all check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about the MCU are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

